{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>A dwelling-place of the Elohim of old.</b> The heavens are a dwelling-place for the Elohim of old, who preceded all gods and chose heavens for His dwelling and habitation, and beneath His dwelling all the mighty of arm dwell." "<b>The seed of the world.</b> Sihon and Og and the kings of Canaan, who were the power and might of the world — therefore against their will they tremble and shake, and their strength is broken before Him. Always the dread of the exalted is upon the lowly — and the strength and might that is His is for your help." "<b>And He shall drive the enemy from before you, and He shall say.</b> To you: <b>Destroy</b> them." "<b>מענה.</b> Any word that needs a mem at its beginning, He placed a heh at its end (Yevamot 13)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:56.390293277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}